    "q-335259": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335259",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=6x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"170px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\, \\\\ \\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
