    "q-335271": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335271",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-5x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-5y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$*",
      "worked_solution": "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-335271-a",
